{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1290977-combat-mostly-defense","id":1290977,"title":"Combat, mostly Defense.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-22T20:06:35-08:00","id":1290977,"title":"Combat, mostly Defense.","content":"So just last session me and my group had some combat and we're slightly confused as to how defense works. Do you roll only your resistance attribute? This felt like it resulted in very weak defense pools even for quite competent characters. Yet setting the highest of your resistance attributes as a flat value felt similarly too high, and we weren't quite sure, based on reading the book, which was correct.<br /> <br /> So how should this be handled or done?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12093-pixelpuzzler","name":"PixelPuzzler","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T00:52:31-08:00","id":1291031,"title":"","content":"You roll resistance attribute and the successes are added to you defence. But it\u2019s not all that you use, you can use a shield, that add to your defence, you can have armor, that force attackers to spend successes to hurt you and may have some knacks or booms that add to your defence or armor.<br /> <br /> If you think it\u2019s low, you have prety good dice rollers going against you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T06:23:32-08:00","id":1291111,"title":"","content":"Defense is equal to 1+rolled successes on whichever resistance attribute is used to defend. And like Mateus mentioned, there are all manner of things that can be used to bump up armor and/or defense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T18:03:44-08:00","id":1291669,"title":"","content":"So to be clear: At the start of combat (or at the start of each turn of combat?) you roll your highest Resistance Attribute against diff 8, add one to the result, and that equals your Defense --- the difficulty of an opponent's attack. How do the defensive Stunts work? Are your successes on the Attribute roll all considered threshold successes that (by default) you're spending on the Dodge stunt to increase your Defense by one each, with the option to instead spend those successes on the other defensive Stunts instead of adding them to your Defense score directly?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">Amateur dinosaur hunter and extreme weather enthusiast, whose interests include spoken mime, armchair parkour, conspicuous ninjutsu and Schr\u00f6edinger's pentameter\u2014of which this sentence may or may not be an example.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13110-eunomiac","name":"Eunomiac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T18:49:43-08:00","id":1291680,"title":"","content":"As I see, there is a wrong description somewhere...<br /> You should roll defence every turn to the first time you are attacked, and keep the defence for that round. This way you may use the defencive stunts every round but not several times a round.<br /> <br /> In Trinity is more clear about when to roll defence. But it sound like if you have multiple attackers you roll multiple times.<br /> In Scion it sounds more like you roll your defence in the beguinning of the combat and keep it to the end...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T23:27:26-08:00","id":1291731,"title":"","content":"You roll your Defense the first time you get attacked each round. At least that's how I run it.<br /> <br /> And I'm pretty sure I got that clarified by Neall too, so there's that.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Defensive Stunts can be handy, like Ducking for Cover against Ranged attacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T12:43:38-08:00","id":1294836,"title":"","content":"Can anyone give me an example of the defensive stunts being used?<br /> <br /> Thank you","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T13:34:34-08:00","id":1294863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Graylion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1290977-combat-mostly-defense?p=1294836#post1294836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can anyone give me an example of the defensive stunts being used?<br /> <br /> Thank you</div> </div> </div> </div>Two Kung Fu mAsters are fighting, the first prepares the attack.<br /> The second rolls Stamina (4) get really luck with 3 successes. He decides to use it to Roll Away as the attacker have a low (3) composure.<br /> The attacker will attack, but won't be able to hit the other as he rolled away and is out of the reach.<br /> The second now can attack, but first need to get close, so he does a mixed action, as its a pure jump forward and punch. The first now rolls 4 (stamina) and gets 2 success, using both on Dodge Stunt (rising defence to 3). The second rolls Athletic + Might 8 (Colse Combat is higher, bus as he needs to jump forward to reach...) gets 3 successes, one he uses to get close, but the other are not enough to hit the first fighter, resulting in a miss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T13:56:08-08:00","id":1294873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1290977-combat-mostly-defense?p=1294863#post1294863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Two Kung Fu mAsters are fighting, the first prepares the attack.<br /> The second rolls Stamina (4) get really luck with 3 successes. He decides to use it to Roll Away as the attacker have a low (3) composure.<br /> The attacker will attack, but won't be able to hit the other as he rolled away and is out of the reach.<br /> The second now can attack, but first need to get close, so he does a mixed action, as its a pure jump forward and punch. The first now rolls 4 (stamina) and gets 2 success, using both on Dodge Stunt (rising defence to 3). The second rolls Athletic + Might 8 (Colse Combat is higher, bus as he needs to jump forward to reach...) gets 3 successes, one he uses to get close, but the other are not enough to hit the first fighter, resulting in a miss.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So the Dodge Stunt in the base reflexive action of rolling your defense pool the first time you are attacked and applying successes to your static defense for the round. Silly enough I just didnt realize it was the &quot;Dodge Stunt&quot;.<br /> Is there a full defense or total defense that allows you to dodge only and NOT take to simple action?<br /> <br /> Thanks","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T19:20:33-08:00","id":1294952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Graylion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1290977-combat-mostly-defense?p=1294873#post1294873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So the Dodge Stunt in the base reflexive action of rolling your defense pool the first time you are attacked and applying successes to your static defense for the round. Silly enough I just didnt realize it was the &amp;quot;Dodge Stunt&amp;quot;.<br /> Is there a full defense or total defense that allows you to dodge only and NOT take to simple action?<br /> <br /> Thanks</div> </div> </div> </div>If you decide to gondefence, you use your action to defend yourself and by doing that you double the number of dice you roll for defence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T23:14:47-08:00","id":1294980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Graylion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1290977-combat-mostly-defense?p=1294836#post1294836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can anyone give me an example of the defensive stunts being used?<br /> <br /> Thank you</div> </div> </div> </div>Another Stunt:<br /> <br /> Frankie &quot;Bullets&quot; Malone, Chicago Hitman, opens fire with his tommy gun and gets three successes on the attack. Andromeda, Scion of Loki, decides to get her head down. When she rolls Composure, she gets two successes. She spends one of them to use the &quot;Dive For Cover&quot; Stunt to scramble behind the bar's counter, which the SG rules makes for Light Cover.<br /> <br /> Light cover, as per the Origin book, can absorb four damage before breaking. Assuming Andromeda's player pumps up their defense to 2 from the remaining success, the enemy has 1 threshold success. The Inflict Injury stunt that Malone gets for 0s is applied to the cover, so it can take three more Injuries before breaking. The SG also applies the Pin Stunt with the last Success, so Andromeda's player will need to buy off a level 2 complication when returning fire on the next round, or else will take an automatic injury.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T10:18:48-08:00","id":1295076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1290977-combat-mostly-defense?p=1294863#post1294863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Two Kung Fu mAsters are fighting, the first prepares the attack.<br /> The second rolls Stamina (4) get really luck with 3 successes. He decides to use it to Roll Away as the attacker have a low (3) composure.<br /> The attacker will attack, but won't be able to hit the other as he rolled away and is out of the reach.<br /> The second now can attack, but first need to get close, so he does a mixed action, as its a pure jump forward and punch. The first now rolls 4 (stamina) and gets 2 success, using both on Dodge Stunt (rising defence to 3). The second rolls Athletic + Might 8 (Colse Combat is higher, bus as he needs to jump forward to reach...) gets 3 successes, one he uses to get close, but the other are not enough to hit the first fighter, resulting in a miss.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;Over unexceptional terrain, characters can move<br /> between near and clash range at will without any<br /> kind of roll or extra action.&quot; p.80<br /> <br /> So, no need to mix actions for attacking and moving.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T10:50:38-08:00","id":1295083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1290977-combat-mostly-defense?p=1295076#post1295076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Over unexceptional terrain, characters can move<br /> between near and clash range at will without any<br /> kind of roll or extra action.&amp;quot; p.80<br /> <br /> So, no need to mix actions for attacking and moving.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, when Inwas writing I thought, why can\u2019t the first reach and the second can, than I remembered the mixed action and used it, but it\u2019s not necessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T03:45:25-07:00","id":1297680,"title":"","content":"What kind of defence numbers are people seeing? And what kind f enhancements are people allowing on Defence rolls?<br /> <br /> My players are now Legend 3 and getting 3-4 defence most of the time (1+rolled resistance +soft armour)<br /> <br /> This doesn\u2019t really stop Rivals, Nemeses and Titanspawn from hitting them but does reduce the number of stunts those enemies can perform. Rivals may need to have some kind of magic, stunts or teamwork to meet those defences<br /> <br /> I have a player looking at making an Intangibility type power (ghosts, death, etc) and getting a +2e on defence rolls which would bring them to reliably defence 6 or 7 and I\u2019m wondering if that\u2019s going to start really straining what the opposition can hope to reach.<br /> <br /> Nemesis has 11 dice primary so averages about 3-4 successes, maybe 1-2 enhancement from a relic they have or an blessing from somewhere and it\u2019s 4-6 so enough to deal a damage and maybe add in a stunt.<br /> <br /> Yes I can use non physical threats to threaten this PC, but it gets a bit stale if they repeatedly find themselves facing that kind of foe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}